# expect: 100
# expect: 200
# expect: 300
# expect: dyn
# expect: ok
# Phase 2: for-loop over [Arr i64] (a wide scalar). The binding stays DYN
# (not narrowed) — wide for-binding narrowing is the deferred wide-cell + SM
# work (NOT_IMPLEMENTED §4). Iteration still yields correct values (OP_ARR_GET
# pushes raw wide bits, which are boxed before binding). For typed wide
# arithmetic, use a while loop + arr-get, which narrows via Phase 1.
proc main {} {
  def a [[Arr i64] 100 200 300]
  for $a x { print $x }              # 100 200 300 (correct values, boxed)
  for $a y { assert-type $y dyn }    # binding is dyn, not i64
  print "dyn"
  print "ok"
}
main
